    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it just feels so much more honest to say it's over. people talk about \"reclaiming pieces\" like i'm some puzzle that can be fixed. but if the core of who I was is gone, the pieces don't even fit anymore. it's like trying to put a soul back into a body that was only ever meant to be a vessel for something else. if the vessel is broken and the contents are spilled, shouldn't the story just end there? why keep pretending there's something worth preserving?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
